Subject: tqt3integration: let the build set TQT_PLUGINS_DIR

The plugins directory came from `pkg-config --variable=pluginsdir`,
which in a cross build returns the value prefixed with
PKG_CONFIG_SYSROOT_DIR -- the build host's sysroot path.  It is the
install destination of libtqttde, so the plugin was staged under
<DESTDIR>/<build-host path>/opt/trinity/plugins, and it becomes
TQTTDELIBDIR in the generated TQt-side tqttdeintegration_x11.cpp.  Keep the pkg-config query as the default but let
-DTQT_PLUGINS_DIR override it.

---
--- a/tqt3integration/ConfigureChecks.cmake	2026-09-29 02:39:18.718809768 -0500
+++ b/tqt3integration/ConfigureChecks.cmake	2026-09-29 02:39:26.024206355 -0500
@@ -12,9 +12,15 @@
 
 ##### check for tqt plugins dir #################
 
-execute_process(
-  COMMAND ${PKG_CONFIG_EXECUTABLE}
-    tqt-mt --variable=pluginsdir
-  OUTPUT_VARIABLE TQT_PLUGINS_DIR
-  OUTPUT_STRIP_TRAILING_WHITESPACE
-)
+# A cross build's pkg-config prefixes PKG_CONFIG_SYSROOT_DIR onto path
+# variables, so pluginsdir comes back as the build-host sysroot path; it is
+# both the install destination and a path compiled into the library.  Let
+# the build pass the target path instead.
+if( NOT TQT_PLUGINS_DIR )
+  execute_process(
+    COMMAND ${PKG_CONFIG_EXECUTABLE}
+      tqt-mt --variable=pluginsdir
+    OUTPUT_VARIABLE TQT_PLUGINS_DIR
+    OUTPUT_STRIP_TRAILING_WHITESPACE
+  )
+endif( )
